<title>USA: IADB says sets new lending rates for 2nd half 1997.</title>
<headline>IADB says sets new lending rates for 2nd half 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Inter-American Development Bank said on Thursday it was setting new lending rates on the convertible currency part of loans from ordinary capital for the second half of 1997.</p>
<p>The bank said the second-half lending rate would be 6.59 percent for outstanding balances of currency-pool loans approved after January 1, 1990, down from 6.68 percent in the first half.</p>
<p>The rate for disbursements on loans approved between January 1 1983 and December 31 1989 would rise to 6.97 percent, from 6.73 percent in the first half.</p>
<p>Other changes were as follows:</p>
<p>			     2nd half 1997	    1st half 1997</p>
<p> Dollar loans	    6.97 pct		   6.90 pct</p>
<p> Mark loans		6.66 pct		   6.95 pct</p>
<p> Yen loans		 3.37 pct		   3.69 pct</p>
<p> Swiss franc loans     4.58 pct		   4.98 pct</p>
</text>
